---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import GuideList from "../../components/GuideList.astro";
import Simple from "../../layouts/Simple.astro";
import { visitIdsForArticle } from "../../data/catalog";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles", ({ data }) => data.section === "compare")).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);
---
<Simple
  title="Analytics Tools Compared Side by Side"
  description="Analytics tools compared side by side: DataFast, Plausible, Fathom, Google Analytics, PostHog, Mixpanel, and Amplitude, with pricing and who each one fits."
  kicker="Compare"
  lede="Compare DataFast with Plausible, Fathom, Google Analytics, PostHog, Mixpanel, and Amplitude. Each page covers pricing, features, and which tool fits your site."
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Compare" }]}
>
  <p>Use a comparison when you are choosing between two products, not when you are leaving one without a replacement in mind. Prices on these pages are as of 26 November 2026. The <a href="/reviews/datafast/">DataFast review</a> explains that product. The <a href="/pricing/datafast/">DataFast pricing</a> page lists its plans. The <a href="/alternatives/">alternatives</a> hub is the place to start when you want to leave a tool.</p>
  <section slot="wide" class="band band-yellow">
    <div class="article-wide">
      <h2>Analytics tools compared</h2>
      <GuideList
        items={articles.map((article) => ({
          href: `/${article.id}/`,
          title: article.data.title,
          description: article.data.description,
          visits: visitIdsForArticle(article.id),
        }))}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</Simple>
